+### PI-Desktop
+
+```bash
+trellis init -u your-name --pi-desktop
+```
+
+PI-Desktop is extension-backed and reuses the Pi Agent surface. Trellis writes the same prompts, agents, and skills, then the host loads the plugin wrapper from `.pi-desktop/` and injects task context before `Bash` commands and sub-agent runs.
+
+Layout:
+
+- `.pi-desktop/trellis/manifest.json` + `.pi-desktop/trellis/main.js`: the plugin wrapper the host loads; `contributes.agentExtensions` registers `agent/index.ts`
+- `.pi-desktop/trellis/agent/index.ts`: session context, `Bash` `TRELLIS_CONTEXT_ID` propagation, and sub-agent JSONL injection
+- `.pi/prompts/trellis-{name}.md`: session-boundary prompts (`finish-work`, `continue`; `start` only where applicable) — the same files Pi Agent reads
+- `.pi/agents/{name}.md`: `trellis-implement`, `trellis-check`, `trellis-research` via host sub-agent discovery — the same files Pi Agent reads
+- `.agents/skills/trellis-{name}/SKILL.md`: the five Trellis workflow skills (shared layer) — the same files Pi Agent reads
+
+PI-Desktop ships no `settings.json` of its own: runtime behavior comes from the plugin at `.pi-desktop/trellis/agent/index.ts`. Sub-agents are dispatched through the host `Task` tool, and the shell tool is `Bash` (the shell behind it is user-configurable: PowerShell, cmd, git-bash, or bash). `trellis pi-desktop {install,status,uninstall}` manages the plugin, and global sub-agents go to `~/.agents/subagents`.
+
